{"id":"n2-065","title":"～ずにはいられない","romaji":"〜zu ni wa irarenai","jlptLevel":2,"shortExplanation":"Cannot help but; cannot resist doing; an irresistible urge.","longExplanation":"The ～ずにはいられない grammar point expresses that one cannot resist or help doing something. In other words, there is a strong urge that one cannot suppress. It's formed from the negative stem of a verb plus ずにはいられない. (Note: する -> せずにはいられない.)","formation":"Verb-ない form (drop ない) + ずにはいられない","examples":[{"jp":"この曲を聞くと、歌わずにはいられない。","romaji":"Kono kyoku o kiku to, utawazu ni wa irarenai.","en":"When I hear this song, I can’t help but sing.","words":[{"surface":"この","vocabId":null},{"surface":"曲","vocabId":"1239700","reading":"きょく"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"聞くと","vocabId":"1591110","reading":"きくと","baseForm":"聞く"},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"歌わ","vocabId":"1588120","reading":"うたう","baseForm":"歌う"},{"surface":"ず","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ぬ"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"い","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"いる"},{"surface":"られ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"られる"},{"surface":"ない","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[6,7,8,9,10,11]},{"jp":"彼女が泣いているのを見ると、慰めずにはいられない。","romaji":"Kanojo ga naite iru no o miru to, nagusamezu ni wa irarenai.","en":"When I see her crying, I can’t resist comforting her.","words":[{"surface":"彼女","vocabId":"1483150","reading":"かのじょ"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"泣いている","vocabId":"1229840","reading":"ないている","baseForm":"泣く"},{"surface":"の","vocabId":null},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"見ると","vocabId":"1259290","reading":"みると","baseForm":"見る"},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"慰め","vocabId":"1156880","reading":"なぐさめ","baseForm":"慰める"},{"surface":"ず","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ぬ"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"い","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"いる"},{"surface":"られ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"られる"},{"surface":"ない","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[8,9,10,11,12,13]},{"jp":"この小説は面白いので、読まずにはいられない。","romaji":"Kono shousetsu wa omoshiroi no de, yomazu ni wa irarenai.","en":"This novel is so interesting that I can’t help but read it.","words":[{"surface":"この","vocabId":null},{"surface":"小説","vocabId":"1348430","reading":"しょうせつ"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"面白いので","vocabId":"1533580","reading":"おもしろいので","baseForm":"面白い"},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"読ま","vocabId":"1456360","reading":"よむ","baseForm":"読む"},{"surface":"ず","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ぬ"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"い","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"いる"},{"surface":"られ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"られる"},{"surface":"ない","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[6,7,8,9,10,11]},{"jp":"彼はおいしい料理を前にすると、食べずにはいられない。","romaji":"Kare wa oishii ryouri o mae ni suru to, tabezu ni wa irarenai.","en":"When he’s faced with delicious food, he can’t help but eat it.","words":[{"surface":"彼","vocabId":"1483070","reading":"かれ"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"おいしい","vocabId":"1486650","reading":"おいしい"},{"surface":"料理","vocabId":"1554310","reading":"りょうり"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"前に","vocabId":"1392590","reading":"まえに"},{"surface":"する","vocabId":null},{"surface":"と","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"食べ","vocabId":"1358280","reading":"たべる","baseForm":"食べる"},{"surface":"ず","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ぬ"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"い","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"いる"},{"surface":"られ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"られる"},{"surface":"ない","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[10,11,12,13,14,15]}],"formalityLevel":"very-formal-literary","usageNote":"\"Cannot resist doing/an irresistible urge\" - the everyday version of the overwhelming-feeling idea.","family":{"id":"cant-help-but","name":